Hi, I'm Ryan Rover.

2
00:00:01,956 --> 00:00:04,313
Here's a question most people never ask.

3
00:00:04,493 --> 00:00:06,991
Your credit card gives you rewards,

4
00:00:06,991 --> 00:00:07,776
a free app,

5
00:00:07,776 --> 00:00:11,273
fraud protection, sometimes even airport lounges.

6
00:00:11,453 --> 00:00:13,241
So who's paying for all of that?

7
00:00:13,421 --> 00:00:15,766
Because the card company isn't a charity.

8
00:00:15,946 --> 00:00:17,677
Today, we follow the money,

9
00:00:17,677 --> 00:00:19,856
and we find out exactly how credit

10
00:00:19,856 --> 00:00:22,099
card companies make money from you.

11
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:23,781
In twenty twenty two,

12
00:00:23,781 --> 00:00:27,204
according to the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau,

13
00:00:27,204 --> 00:00:30,310
credit card companies charged Americans more than

14
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:32,845
one hundred billion dollars in interest,

15
00:00:32,845 --> 00:00:35,507
plus around twenty five billion dollars in

16
00:00:35,507 --> 00:00:35,824
fees.

17
00:00:36,175 --> 00:00:37,301
That's not a typo.

18
00:00:37,481 --> 00:00:39,979
More than one hundred billion dollars in

19
00:00:39,979 --> 00:00:40,854
a single year,

20
00:00:40,854 --> 00:00:41,916
just in interest.

21
00:00:42,096 --> 00:00:43,815
And that's before we count the money

22
00:00:43,815 --> 00:00:45,486
merchants pay every time you swipe.

23
00:00:45,666 --> 00:00:47,606
Credit cards are one of the most

24
00:00:47,606 --> 00:00:49,485
profitable products in banking.

25
00:00:49,665 --> 00:00:52,006
Once you understand how that profit is

26
00:00:52,006 --> 00:00:54,039
made, you can use cards for their

27
00:00:54,039 --> 00:00:56,318
benefits while paying almost nothing.

28
