830
00:25:52,437 --> 00:25:53,493
Same card.

831
00:25:53,673 --> 00:25:54,892
Same rewards.

832
00:25:55,072 --> 00:25:56,500
Opposite outcomes.

833
00:25:56,850 --> 00:25:59,165
Same card, same spending,

834
00:25:59,165 --> 00:26:00,368
same rewards.

835
00:26:00,548 --> 00:26:02,499
The only difference is paying in full.

836
00:26:02,848 --> 00:26:04,172
And here's the twist.

837
00:26:04,352 --> 00:26:07,012
Jordan's interest helps pay for the system

838
00:26:07,012 --> 00:26:08,659
that funds Alex's rewards.

839
00:26:08,839 --> 00:26:11,289
That's the quiet truth of credit cards.

840
00:26:11,469 --> 00:26:13,451
The people who pay in full are,

841
00:26:13,451 --> 00:26:14,026
in a way,

842
00:26:14,026 --> 00:26:16,264
subsidized by the people who don't.

843
00:26:16,444 --> 00:26:18,055
The goal of this video is to

844
00:26:18,055 --> 00:26:20,240
move you from Jordan's side to Alex's.

845
00:26:20,590 --> 00:26:22,893
Let's do the honest math on premium

846
00:26:22,893 --> 00:26:25,130
